2025-05-01 03:25:37 - Thread-1390 (execute) - INFO - [Corrected SQL]
```sql
/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Goal  
   ----- 
   Compare every salesperson’s annual total sales with the sum of his / her
   monthly sales‑quota for the same calendar year, then compute the difference
   (sales – quota).  The required information lives in two tables:

     • salesorderheader (each order → subtotal, salespersonid, orderdate)
     • SalesPersonQuotaHistory (one row per salesperson per month)

   Steps / reasoning  
   -----------------
   1.  Convert each date to its calendar year with strftime('%Y', …).
   2.  Aggregate:
         a) sales:   SUM(subtotal)  per salesperson‑year
         b) quota:   SUM(SalesQuota) per salesperson‑year
   3.  SQLite lacks FULL OUTER JOIN, so to combine the sets we:
         • LEFT JOIN sales → quota   (keeps all sales rows, adds quota when exists)
         • UNION the quota rows that did not find a matching sales row.
   4.  Calculate the difference using COALESCE to treat missing values as 0.
   5.  Order the final list for readability.  (Remove LIMIT to see everything.)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
WITH
sales AS (
    SELECT
        salespersonid,
        strftime('%Y', orderdate) AS year,
        SUM(subtotal)             AS yearly_sales
    FROM salesorderheader
    GROUP BY salespersonid, strftime('%Y', orderdate)
),
quota AS (
    SELECT
        BusinessEntityID          AS salespersonid,
        strftime('%Y', QuotaDate) AS year,
        SUM(SalesQuota)           AS yearly_quota
    FROM SalesPersonQuotaHistory
    GROUP BY BusinessEntityID, strftime('%Y', QuotaDate)
)

-- (a) every sales row + any matching quota
SELECT
    s.salespersonid,
    s.year,
    s.yearly_sales,
    q.yearly_quota,
    COALESCE(s.yearly_sales,0) - COALESCE(q.yearly_quota,0) AS sales_minus_quota
FROM sales AS s
LEFT JOIN quota AS q
  ON s.salespersonid = q.salespersonid
 AND s.year          = q.year

UNION ALL

-- (b) quota rows that had no matching sales row
SELECT
    q.salespersonid,
    q.year,
    NULL                      AS yearly_sales,
    q.yearly_quota,
    0 - COALESCE(q.yearly_quota,0)         AS sales_minus_quota
FROM quota AS q
LEFT JOIN sales AS s
  ON q.salespersonid = s.salespersonid
 AND q.year          = s.year
WHERE s.salespersonid IS NULL      -- quota‑only rows

ORDER BY salespersonid, year;
```
